The two rewritten fit-count assertions follow from the new semantics: three TS points from a stale GP cost three fits; an explicit refit followed by four PI points costs four fits total. I also found two material issues: executable prompts still say global/local actions do not fit, and BoTorch 0.18.1’s PES/MES training-input handling mixes coordinate systems when normalization is enabled.
