The h2 stamp is appropriate; the utility formula and weights are unchanged, so I don’t see a separate utility-version bump as necessary. The replay entry points do need a version guard: they currently accept h1 records and run the h2 executor. Keeping the old `seed` field preserves parsing compatibility, not historical replay behavior.
